136 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 129 0 R
/E (TJ IOI is a computer science competition for high school and middle school students in the DC metropolitan area, run by the Computer Team at TJHSST. Students compete in groups of three to solve competitive programming problems. Our goal is to incite passion for computer science in a friendly, teamwork-focused environment.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
137 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 129 0 R
/E (Although many high schoolers have taken computer science courses at their schools, they may lack other avenues to pursue their study of computer science. Moreover, many middle schoolers do not have access to computer science courses at all. We aim to provide such an opportunity by exposing competitors to advanced algorithms and data structures that go beyond the curriculum of AP Computer Science.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
138 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 129 0 R
/E (Last year, ~100 in-person participants competed. We awarded $500 in prizes to top teams. Over the past few years, TJCT has hosted more than 1000 participants at competitions.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
139 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 129 0 R
/E (Why do we need your support?)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
140 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 129 0 R
/E (We will award prizes to the top teams and provide lunch, stickers, and certificates to contestants, coaches, and volunteers. We will also be paying for use of the TJHSST building and custodial services. Your sponsorship provides the crucial financial support needed for making this exciting competition a reality. Based on your contribution, we would be happy to recognize your organization as described in the table below.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
